guide forever/professions/leatherworking
title Leatherworking 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Leatherworking` from Era-baseline data:
# Blizzard Classic Era client tables (recipes, skill thresholds, reagents,
# vendor prices) via wago.tools, pfQuest (vendors, drops, nodes) and a curated
# trainer list checked against npcs.json. Nothing public confirms Forever
# changed profession recipes, so the Era recipe list is the baseline.
#
# Trainers and vendors are smart targets: the engine sends each character to
# the nearest one of its faction. Farming spots are picked per faction.
#
# Recipe choice: cheapest expected cost to 300 (Classic skill-up chances:
# certain while orange, falling from yellow to grey), with gathered materials
# valued at 4x their vendor sell price; see tools/lib/professions/plan.js.
# Material counts are expected values; yellow and green crafts can take more.
#
# Route:
#     1-52  Light Armor Kit (about 68)
#    52-60  Handstitched Leather Boots (about 17)
#    60-75  Small Leather Ammo Pouch (about 21)
#    75-85  Embossed Leather Cloak (about 10)
#    85-110 Embossed Leather Gloves (about 52)
#   110-130 Fine Leather Belt (about 32)
#   130-145 Light Leather Pants (about 27)
#   145-150 Nimble Leather Gloves (about 6)
#   150-155 Heavy Leather (about 7)
#   155-170 Hillman's Shoulders (about 23)
#   170-180 Hillman's Leather Gloves (about 13)
#   180-195 Green Leather Belt (about 27)
#   195-200 Barbaric Shoulders (about 6)
#   200-210 Green Leather Bracers (about 14)
#   210-225 Guardian Gloves (about 27)
#   225-240 Nightscape Headband (about 27)
#   240-245 Turtle Scale Breastplate (about 13)
#   245-250 Thick Leather Ammo Pouch (about 6)
#   250-261 Rugged Armor Kit (about 16)
#   261-292 Wicked Leather Gauntlets (about 37)
#   292-300 Runic Leather Headband (about 8)

step Apprentice Leatherworking
  tip Leatherworking runs alongside leveling. Forever's Legacy System rewards crafting professions at skill 150, 225 and 300 (the Journeyman, Expert and Artisan caps), so each of those checkpoints counts. Materials for 1-75 are worth about 1g 7s in all.
  train Leatherworking Apprentice
  skill Leatherworking 1
  buy 2320 x101 nearest

step Light Leather (Alliance)
  only Alliance
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Skin Crag Boar, Elder Crag Boar, Ice Claw Bear, Juvenile Snow Leopard, Large Crag Boar, Scarred Crag Boar, Snow Leopard, Snow Tracker Wolf, Winter Wolf, Young Black Bear here (beasts of level 5-20 yield it); the Skinning guide routes this. The Auction House works too.
  collect 2318 x165 @34.3,55.6 era

step Light Leather (Horde)
  only Horde
  zone Durotar
  tip Skin Armored Scorpid, Bloodtalon Scythemaw, Bloodtalon Taillasher, Clattering Scorpid, Dire Mottled Boar, Dreadmaw Crocolisk, Durotar Tiger, Elder Mottled Boar, Thunder Lizard, Venomtail Scorpid here (beasts of level 5-20 yield it); the Skinning guide routes this. The Auction House works too.
  collect 2318 x165 @37.5,32.4 era

step Light Armor Kit to 52
  zone Azeroth
  tip Orange (a point every craft) until 30, yellow until 45, green until 60.
  craft 2152 until 52

step Handstitched Leather Boots to 60
  tip Yellow until 55, green until 70: not every craft gives a point.
  craft 2149 until 60

step Leatherworking recipes at 60
  tip Back to a Leatherworking trainer: Small Leather Ammo Pouch is taught from Leatherworking 60.
  learn 9062

step Small Leather Ammo Pouch to 75
  tip Yellow until 75, green until 90: not every craft gives a point. 75 is the Apprentice cap.
  craft 9062 until 75
  skill Leatherworking 75

